{"id":"weight","cards":[{"id":"weight604e418b","l":1,"f":"<b>Diet</b>?","b":"the goal is <b>caloric reduction</b> — total calorie restriction matters more than macronutrient composition; intensive programmes give ~<b>4–5 kg</b>; regain is common when support stops.","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weightede07e29","l":1,"f":"<b>Exercise</b>?","b":"≥ <b>150 min/week</b> moderate aerobic activity; potentiates diet.","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight5ac19ff2","l":1,"f":"<b>Psychological</b>?","b":"<b>CBT</b> most used; modest alone, useful in a multimodal approach.","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight18bf23df","l":1,"f":"<b>Drugs</b>?","b":"indications: <b>BMI &gt; 30, or &gt; 27 with comorbidities</b>, or inadequate loss/regain after lifestyle change or surgery; <b>stop if no significant loss after 3 months</b>.","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight872cc379","l":1,"f":"<b>Phentermine</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Sympathomimetic (↑ NE, dopamine); <b>short-term ≤ 3 months</b>","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight7f804235","l":1,"f":"<b>Phentermine</b> — Total body weight loss?","b":"5–6%","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weightafb0dbae","l":1,"f":"<b>Phentermine</b> — Side effects?","b":"↑ HR, hypertension, dry mouth, insomnia","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight678c32a1","l":1,"f":"<b>Orlistat</b> — Mechanism?","b":"<b>Inhibits pancreatic and gastric lipase</b> → ↓ fat absorption","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weightc410b559","l":1,"f":"<b>Orlistat</b> — Total body weight loss?","b":"5–10%","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weightbbbab528","l":1,"f":"<b>Orlistat</b> — Side effects?","b":"Diarrhoea, faecal incontinence, flatulence","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weightcfea43d4","l":1,"f":"<b>Phentermine/topiramate</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Appetite suppressant + topiramate","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight22cdf183","l":1,"f":"<b>Phentermine/topiramate</b> — Total body weight loss?","b":"7–10%","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weightbe88813d","l":1,"f":"<b>Phentermine/topiramate</b> — Side effects?","b":"Headache, paraesthesia, dry mouth","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight796d9905","l":1,"f":"<b>Bupropion/naltrexone</b> — Mechanism?","b":"↑ hypothalamic α-MSH → appetite suppression","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weightc56c84b0","l":1,"f":"<b>Bupropion/naltrexone</b> — Total body weight loss?","b":"5–6%","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight2faca28f","l":1,"f":"<b>Bupropion/naltrexone</b> — Side effects?","b":"Headache, insomnia, tremor, constipation","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight76230d0e","l":1,"f":"<b>Lorcaserin</b> — Mechanism?","b":"5-HT2C agonist","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight9eb9db2d","l":1,"f":"<b>Lorcaserin</b> — Total body weight loss?","b":"5–7%","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight9bdea915","l":1,"f":"<b>Lorcaserin</b> — Side effects?","b":"Hallucinations, headache, CV risk","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight3d443c5a","l":1,"f":"<b>Liraglutide</b> — Mechanism?","b":"<b>GLP-1 agonist</b> → satiety, insulin sensitivity","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weightacfbd4ab","l":1,"f":"<b>Liraglutide</b> — Total body weight loss?","b":"7–9%","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight34df73be","l":1,"f":"<b>Liraglutide</b> — Side effects?","b":"Nausea, diarrhoea, rare pancreatitis","c":"Non-surgical treatment"},{"id":"weight4a1983e6","l":1,"f":"<b>Laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy (LSG)</b>?","b":"<b>most performed today</b>; removes <b>75–80%</b> of the stomach; restrictive + <b>↓ ghrelin</b>; simpler, no intestinal rerouting; <b>irreversible, possible long-term reflux</b>.","c":"Bariatric operations › Restrictive"},{"id":"weight75eb144a","l":1,"f":"<b>Adjustable gastric band (LAGB)</b>?","b":"silicone band → <b>30-mL pouch</b>, adjusted via a saline port; least invasive, reversible; <b>high failure rate</b>, slippage, poor long-term results.","c":"Bariatric operations › Restrictive"},{"id":"weight3a46c5a2","l":1,"f":"<b>Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB)</b>?","b":"<b>gold standard</b>; <b>20–30 mL pouch</b>; restrictive + malabsorptive + hormonal changes that improve <b>diabetes</b>; alimentary limb 100–150 cm, biliopancreatic limb 30–60 cm, common channel; better long-term weight loss; deficiencies, dumping, more complex.","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight7af7bd50","l":1,"f":"<b>BPD/duodenal switch</b>?","b":"<b>most malabsorptive</b> (sleeve + long bypass); <b>highest weight loss and diabetes resolution</b>; severe malnutrition.","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight9771b136","l":1,"f":"<b>SADI</b>?","b":"sleeve + single duodeno-ileal anastomosis — simpler BPD/DS; still investigational.","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weightacf63039","l":1,"f":"<b>Jejunoileal bypass (historical)</b>?","b":"bypassed 90–95% of the small bowel → malnutrition, diarrhoea, <b>liver failure</b>.","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight1d3b4674","l":1,"f":"<b>Procedure LSG</b> — Expected %EWL?","b":"40–70%","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight9a61ba32","l":1,"f":"<b>Procedure LSG</b> — Key benefit?","b":"Simple, preserves digestion","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight9033ad2b","l":1,"f":"<b>Procedure LSG</b> — Key risk?","b":"<b>GERD</b>, regain","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight9ec60a2a","l":1,"f":"<b>RYGB</b> — Expected %EWL?","b":"<b>60–80%</b>","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight6f4b49b0","l":1,"f":"<b>RYGB</b> — Key benefit?","b":"Gold standard, metabolic benefit","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight4cbaf2c8","l":1,"f":"<b>RYGB</b> — Key risk?","b":"Dumping, vitamin deficiencies","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight84c14049","l":1,"f":"<b>BPD/DS</b> — Expected %EWL?","b":"70–90%","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weightb76289f6","l":1,"f":"<b>BPD/DS</b> — Key benefit?","b":"Best for diabetes, most weight loss","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight15623a80","l":1,"f":"<b>BPD/DS</b> — Key risk?","b":"Severe malnutrition","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weighte1ab96f4","l":1,"f":"<b>LAGB</b> — Expected %EWL?","b":"30–50%","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weightd376e764","l":1,"f":"<b>LAGB</b> — Key benefit?","b":"Reversible, least invasive","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weighta87f474d","l":1,"f":"<b>LAGB</b> — Key risk?","b":"High failure","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weighta182b4bc","l":1,"f":"<b>SADI</b> — Expected %EWL?","b":"60–80%","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight1fced9aa","l":1,"f":"<b>SADI</b> — Key benefit?","b":"Fewer complications than BPD/DS","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight157698c5","l":1,"f":"<b>SADI</b> — Key risk?","b":"Little long-term data","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight1cbd88df","l":1,"f":"<b>Choosing</b>?","b":"BMI &gt; 50 → RYGB, BPD/DS or SADI · <b>diabetes/metabolic syndrome → RYGB or BPD/DS</b> · simple/low-risk → LSG or LAGB.","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weight0d0e938f","l":2,"f":"Diabetes is the comorbidity that points to <b>RYGB</b>; <b>GERD/oesophagitis</b>","b":"<b>RYGB</b> rather than sleeve","c":"Bariatric operations › Malabsorptive & mixed"},{"id":"weightc0118065","l":1,"f":"<b>Bleeding</b> — Cause?","b":"Staple line/anastomosis","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight8b72fa48","l":1,"f":"<b>Bleeding</b> — Management?","b":"Observe, transfuse, surgery if needed","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weightb7353adf","l":1,"f":"<b>SSI/abscess</b> — Management?","b":"Antibiotics, drainage","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight0a6f2e65","l":1,"f":"<b>Leak (most serious)</b> — Cause?","b":"Staple line/anastomosis failure","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight05057183","l":1,"f":"<b>Leak (most serious)</b> — Management?","b":"<b>Urgent surgery, drainage, antibiotics</b>","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight2f6bd751","l":1,"f":"<b>Early (≤ 30 days) PE</b> — Cause?","b":"Immobility","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight9f90f6c8","l":1,"f":"<b>Early (≤ 30 days) PE</b> — Management?","b":"Early ambulation, anticoagulation","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight4c188ce3","l":1,"f":"<b>Delayed gastric emptying</b> — Cause?","b":"Vagal injury, inflammation","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight149d5563","l":1,"f":"<b>Delayed gastric emptying</b> — Management?","b":"Fluids, prokinetics","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight77eda194","l":1,"f":"<b>Leak</b>?","b":"RYGB — usually the <b>gastrojejunostomy</b>; LSG — the long staple line. <b>Signs: unexplained tachycardia, fever, leukocytosis.</b> <b>Diagnosis: CT with contrast.</b>","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weightd9eebff9","l":2,"f":"Tachycardia after a sleeve = <b>leak</b> until proven otherwise; unstable leak → <b>operate</b>; stable","b":"drain (CT first)","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight62d87fdb","l":1,"f":"<b>Band slippage/erosion</b> — Procedure?","b":"LAGB","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weightb24a1462","l":1,"f":"<b>Band slippage/erosion</b> — Management?","b":"Removal/revision","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight1caf3d7c","l":1,"f":"<b>Stricture at the gastrojejunostomy</b> — Procedure?","b":"RYGB","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight39da2d80","l":1,"f":"<b>Stricture at the gastrojejunostomy</b> — Management?","b":"<b>Endoscopic dilatation</b>","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight7980939a","l":1,"f":"<b>Marginal ulcer</b> — Procedure?","b":"RYGB","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight0bd6aca3","l":1,"f":"<b>Marginal ulcer</b> — Management?","b":"PPIs, diet (avoid <b>NSAIDs</b>, smoking)","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weightcf4d9d88","l":1,"f":"<b>Dumping</b> — Procedure?","b":"RYGB, BPD/DS","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight27438b27","l":1,"f":"<b>Dumping</b> — Management?","b":"Low-carb small meals, acarbose","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weightd37e27e4","l":1,"f":"<b>Malnutrition</b> — Procedure?","b":"BPD/DS, RYGB","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weightdb6c1bef","l":1,"f":"<b>Malnutrition</b> — Management?","b":"Lifelong supplements","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weighta75dc3a8","l":1,"f":"<b>Internal hernia (life-threatening)</b> — Procedure?","b":"RYGB","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight0b8ba57a","l":1,"f":"<b>Internal hernia (life-threatening)</b> — Management?","b":"<b>Urgent surgery</b>; prevent by closing mesenteric defects (Petersen's)","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight9f0e0d41","l":2,"f":"After RYGB: progressive dysphagia (solids → liquids) → <b>stricture</b>; epigastric pain/bleeding → <b>marginal ulcer (NSAIDs)</b>; intermittent obstruction","b":"<b>internal hernia</b> (CT \"swirl\" of mesenteric vessels)","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight5acfa327","l":1,"f":"<b>Who should avoid surgery</b>?","b":"severe heart/lung disease, <b>untreated psychiatric illness</b> (binge eating, substance abuse), non-compliant patients.","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weight32fc169a","l":2,"f":"Rapid weight loss","b":"<b>gallstones</b>","c":"Outcomes & complications"},{"id":"weightda7e73d7","l":1,"f":"<b>Iron</b> — At risk?","b":"RYGB, BPD/DS","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weightb79d35c7","l":1,"f":"<b>Iron</b> — Cause?","b":"Duodenal bypass, ↓ acid","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight6a9401d2","l":1,"f":"<b>Iron</b> — Result?","b":"Anaemia","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weightd8eb8fa7","l":1,"f":"<b>Nutrient B12</b> — At risk?","b":"RYGB, BPD/DS","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weightb6d402d4","l":1,"f":"<b>Nutrient B12</b> — Cause?","b":"↓ <b>intrinsic factor</b>, duodenal bypass","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight3d611303","l":1,"f":"<b>Nutrient B12</b> — Result?","b":"Anaemia, neuropathy (IM B12 if severe)","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weightd99dc44d","l":1,"f":"<b>Folate</b> — At risk?","b":"All","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weightde910041","l":1,"f":"<b>Folate</b> — Cause?","b":"Low intake","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight1ed8e12c","l":1,"f":"<b>Folate</b> — Result?","b":"Macrocytic anaemia","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight2cb15ebd","l":1,"f":"<b>Vitamin A</b> — At risk?","b":"BPD/DS","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight26392304","l":1,"f":"<b>Vitamin A</b> — Cause?","b":"Fat malabsorption","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weightffb27d16","l":1,"f":"<b>Vitamin A</b> — Result?","b":"Night blindness","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight88682f44","l":1,"f":"<b>Vitamin D / calcium</b> — At risk?","b":"BPD/DS, RYGB","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight448d675d","l":1,"f":"<b>Vitamin D / calcium</b> — Cause?","b":"Fat malabsorption, duodenal bypass","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight461c3316","l":1,"f":"<b>Vitamin D / calcium</b> — Result?","b":"Bone loss, fractures, <b>secondary hyperparathyroidism</b>","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weightb4819863","l":1,"f":"<b>Vitamin K</b> — At risk?","b":"BPD/DS","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight4ce1dde0","l":1,"f":"<b>Vitamin K</b> — Cause?","b":"Fat malabsorption","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight6748faf0","l":1,"f":"<b>Vitamin K</b> — Result?","b":"Bleeding","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weightecad76c2","l":2,"f":"Hyperparathyroidism after bariatric surgery","b":"<b>vitamin D deficiency</b>","c":"Nutrition after surgery"},{"id":"weight1bc56ba3","l":1,"f":"<b>NIH 1991</b>?","b":"<b>BMI ≥ 40</b>, or <b>35–40 + comorbidity</b> (severe OSA, Pickwickian syndrome, cardiovascular disease, severe T2DM, lifestyle limitation), and a realistic understanding of post-op life. Outdated — ignores lower-BMI patients with metabolic disease.","c":"Indications — old and new criteria"},{"id":"weight544abfc4","l":1,"f":"<b>ASMBS / Diabetes Surgery Summit (2012)</b>?","b":"consider surgery at <b>BMI 30–35 with metabolic comorbidity</b> after failed non-surgical treatment.","c":"Indications — old and new criteria"},{"id":"weight4b1dada5","l":1,"f":"<b>T2DM</b>?","b":"BMI ≥ 40 — strongly recommended; 35–40 — poor control despite medication; <b>30–35 — consider if uncontrolled despite optimal therapy</b>.","c":"Indications — old and new criteria"}]}